465	/**
466	 * ACP's rule for extension methods, the custom requests and notifications two peers agree on
467	 * outside the protocol: the method name must start with an underscore ({@code _}), such as
468	 * {@code _example.com/workspace/buffers} (ACP v1, Extensibility). Every extension API of the SDK
469	 * checks names with {@link #requireExtension}: the builders' {@code extRequestHandler} and
470	 * {@code extNotificationHandler}, the facades' {@code sendExtRequest} and
471	 * {@code sendExtNotification}, and the {@code @ExtRequest} and {@code @ExtNotification} annotations
472	 * when an annotated agent is built. So a custom handler can never replace a protocol method, and a
473	 * custom send can never pass for one. Applications call it only to check a name themselves.
474	 *
475	 * <p>How the SDK treats extension methods, the same on both sides:
476	 * <ul>
477	 * <li>A request no handler serves is answered "Method not found" ({@code -32601}); a notification
478	 * no handler serves is ignored, as ACP asks, and logged at DEBUG only.</li>
479	 * <li>Params the peer omitted arrive as an empty object. Params that cannot be read as the
480	 * handler's params type are answered "Invalid params" ({@code -32602}) for a request; for a
481	 * notification the failure is logged and the notification dropped.</li>
482	 * <li>A request handler must produce a result: one that produces none (an empty {@code Mono}, or
483	 * {@code null}) is answered with an internal error ({@code -32603}). Answer with an empty map when
484	 * there is nothing to return.</li>
485	 * <li>When the peer answers {@code "result": null}, the sender's {@code Mono} completes empty and
486	 * the sync API returns {@code null}.</li>
487	 * <li>They are outside ACP's lifecycle: the SDK does not wait for {@code initialize} before sending
488	 * or serving them, and checks no capability. ACP asks peers to advertise their extensions in the
489	 * {@code _meta} of their capabilities.</li>
490	 * </ul>
491	 *
492	 * @author Mark Pollack
493	 */
494	public final class ExtensionMethods {
495	
496		/** The prefix ACP reserves for extension method names: {@value}. */
497		public static final String PREFIX = "_";
498	
499		private ExtensionMethods() {
500		}
501	
502		/**
503		 * Returns whether a method name is an extension method name.
504		 * @param method the method name, or {@code null}
505		 * @return true if it starts with {@value #PREFIX}; false for {@code null}
506		 */
507		public static boolean isExtension(@Nullable String method) {
508			return method != null && method.startsWith(PREFIX);
509		}
510	
511		/**
512		 * Checks that a method name is an extension method name.
513		 * @param method the method name
514		 * @return the method name, unchanged
515		 * @throws IllegalArgumentException if it is null or does not start with {@value #PREFIX}
516		 */
517		public static String requireExtension(@Nullable String method) {
518			if (method == null || !isExtension(method)) {
519				throw new IllegalArgumentException("Extension method names must start with '" + PREFIX
520						+ "' (ACP reserves the other names for the protocol): " + method);
521			}
522			return method;
523		}
524	
